<title>JAPAN: Sanyo to raise nickel-metal hydride battery output.</title>
<headline>Sanyo to raise nickel-metal hydride battery output.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sanyo Electric Co Ltd said on Tuesday that it would boost output of nickel-metal hydride batteries, used for cellular phones and personal computers, by 50 percent to a monthly 18 million units by the end of 1997.</p>
<p>The increase is to cope with increasing demand for the batteries, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Sanyo currently has a share of about 30 percent in the global market for the batteries, he said.</p>
</text>
